body:
The error is caused by:

https://github.com/fastify/fastify/blob/772bfbe012426d4bdffcf743859bb692656cb713/fastify.js#L752

**What is happening?**

That code snippet produces a tree of encapsulated context

```
app
  |- register "fastify" decorated
  |- register "fastify"
      |- register "f"
```

So, when you run the `myAddSchema` function, you add the schema to "fastify decorated" and all the tree, but since the "fastify decorated" instance is the "app instance" itself, it tries to add two times the schema and it breaks.

@SkeLLLa Could you specify better the use case?

Because, to hotfix your problem, you have just to define the instance where add the schema like this:

```js
app.register(
  fp(async (fastify) => {
    fastify.decorate('myAddSchema', function (whereAddTheSchema) {
      console.log('add schema called');
      whereAddTheSchema.addSchema({
        $id: 'sch1',
        type: 'string',
      });
    });
  })
);

app.register(async (fastify) => {
  fastify.register(async (f) => {
    f.myAddSchema(f);
  });
});
```

I'm not sure if the error is that `app` has registered itself as a child or if it is needed a filter on
"some" children before executing the `addSchema` to them.
